import{_ as t,o as a,c as i,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const c=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 738 | Critique of Hang-Up Retirement | General Typology — Five Hang-Up-Retirement Modes","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 738 | Critique of Hang-Up Retirement | General Typology — Five Hang-Up-Retirement Modes","no":738,"module":4,"tags":["Critique of Hang-Up Retirement","Typology","Five Modes","Pseudo-Transcendence","Energy Waste"],"related":["04-Anti-Predation Core Treatise","17-Plane-Transcendent Strong-One Standards","701-Transcendence-Orthodox Definition Overview"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0738_模块4-挂机养老批判-通用类型学五种模式.md","filePath":"en/0738_模块4-挂机养老批判-通用类型学五种模式.md"}'),o={name:"en/0738_模块4-挂机养老批判-通用类型学五种模式.md"};function s(r,e,l,d,g,u){return a(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-738-critique-of-hang-up-retirement-general-typology-—-five-hang-up-retirement-modes" tabindex="-1">Entry 738 | Critique of Hang-Up Retirement | General Typology — Five Hang-Up-Retirement Modes <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-738-critique-of-hang-up-retirement-general-typology-—-five-hang-up-retirement-modes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 738 | Critique of Hang-Up Retirement | General Typology — Five Hang-Up-Retirement Modes&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 04, 17, 701</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-five-ways-to-lie-flat-the-same-root-disease-no-matter-how-they-vary" tabindex="-1">Introduction: five ways to lie flat, the same root disease no matter how they vary <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-five-ways-to-lie-flat-the-same-root-disease-no-matter-how-they-vary" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: five ways to lie flat, the same root disease no matter how they vary&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Entries 734–737 critiqued four concrete samples: Ji-Ning-style closure, Zheng-Zha-style nihilism, Gu-Chensha-style loneliness, talisman-style waste. But hang-up retirement is not an individual protagonist&#39;s accidental choice; it is a <strong>cross-work, cross-plane, cross-setting universal phenomenon</strong>. To systematically oppose it, we must distill its general typology — exactly how many &quot;lying-flat poses&quot; of hang-up retirement? What are each pose&#39;s identifying features, degeneration path, and civilizational cost?</p><p>Six top-level axioms here act as classification rulers: the anti-predation axiom judges each mode&#39;s power source; the republican axiom of Myriad Races judges each mode&#39;s degree of exclusion of Myriad Ranks; the collective ascension axiom judges whether each mode carries Myriad Ranks forward; the causal self-discipline axiom judges whether each mode disturbs causality; the law-first axiom judges whether each mode is self-consistent at the law level.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-overview-of-the-five-hang-up-retirement-modes" tabindex="-1">I. Overview of the Five Hang-Up-Retirement Modes <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-overview-of-the-five-hang-up-retirement-modes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Overview of the Five Hang-Up-Retirement Modes&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Through Alaya Network cluster analysis of histories across planes, hang-up-retirement strong ones may be summarized into five general modes:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Mode Name</th><th>Core Action</th><th>Typical Sample</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A</td><td>Garden-Closure Type</td><td>Build a small world, retire with relatives/friends</td><td>Ji Ning, various Immortal Sovereigns retiring</td></tr><tr><td>B</td><td>Goal-Vacuum Type</td><td>No new goal after punching through enemies</td><td>Zheng Zha, reincarnation-system protagonists&#39; endings</td></tr><tr><td>C</td><td>Single-Bearer Scapegoat Type</td><td>One person carries all karma, lonely self-consumption</td><td>Gu Chensha, compassionate saviors</td></tr><tr><td>D</td><td>Treasure-Sealing Type</td><td>Lock power up, refuse use</td><td>Talisman holders, treasure guardians</td></tr><tr><td>E</td><td>Rule-Auto Type</td><td>Set a set of rules, then wash hands and leave</td><td>Creators who set up Heavenly Dao and leave</td></tr></tbody></table><p>These five modes are not mutually exclusive; a strong one may stack two or three — for example, Gu Chensha is simultaneously C-type and A-type, both single-bearing and closed. But classification should still be by primary type.</p><h2 id="ii-type-a-garden-closure-type" tabindex="-1">II. Type A: Garden-Closure Type <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-type-a-garden-closure-type" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Type A: Garden-Closure Type&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Identifying features</strong>: the strong one dwells long-term in a self-built independent space (small world, cave-heaven, eternal kingdom), maintaining physical and information distance from the original plane&#39;s beings.</p><p><strong>Degeneration path</strong>:</p><ol><li>Early stage: beautifully called &quot;closed-door Dao-enlightenment,&quot; still periodically coming out to handle affairs;</li><li>Mid stage: all affairs handed to subordinates, only hearing reports; information begins to distort;</li><li>Late stage: completely no longer coming out; subordinates become new separatist forces;</li><li>Endgame: the small world decouples from the original plane; the original plane rots in a vacuum.</li></ol><p><strong>Civilizational cost</strong>: the strongest computable power goes offline; the law network loses a key anchor; predatory factions seize the chance.</p><p><strong>Counter-measure</strong>: Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm&#39;s living-anchor system — the strong one must take law-calibration duty for a star sector; his &quot;closed-door Dao-enlightenment&quot; results must be backfilled in real time through the Alaya Network, not offline.</p><h2 id="iii-type-b-goal-vacuum-type" tabindex="-1">III. Type B: Goal-Vacuum Type <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-type-b-goal-vacuum-type" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Type B: Goal-Vacuum Type&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Identifying features</strong>: the strong one&#39;s entire life goals are oppositional (beat some enemy, break some system); after the goal is achieved, he falls into a goal-less state.</p><p><strong>Degeneration path</strong>:</p><ol><li>Early stage: brief emptiness after victory, beautifully called &quot;relaxation&quot;;</li><li>Mid stage: starts finding new enemies to fight, but cannot find a worthy opponent;</li><li>Late stage: attention turns to personal indulgence (food, collecting, reproduction);</li><li>Endgame: becomes a pure hedonist, completely losing interest in public civilizational affairs.</li></ol><p><strong>Civilizational cost</strong>: construction ability is zero, even negative — to seek entertainment he may disturb plane causality.</p><p><strong>Counter-measure</strong>: constructive goal-chain system — the strong one is implanted with long-term civilizational-engineering goals from Sense-Origin Realm onward, so there is no &quot;after fighting, not knowing what to do&quot; problem.</p><h2 id="iv-type-c-single-bearer-scapegoat-type" tabindex="-1">IV. Type C: Single-Bearer Scapegoat Type <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-type-c-single-bearer-scapegoat-type" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Type C: Single-Bearer Scapegoat Type&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Identifying features</strong>: the strong one takes all beings&#39; responsibility, causality, and suffering onto himself, beautifully called &quot;compassion.&quot;</p><p><strong>Degeneration path</strong>:</p><ol><li>Early stage: sincerely wanting to share beings&#39; burden;</li><li>Mid stage: discovering beings are &quot;not up to it,&quot; beginning to despise beings&#39; ability;</li><li>Late stage: changing from &quot;bearing for beings&quot; to &quot;deciding for beings&quot;;</li><li>Endgame: becomes a de facto dictator, yet still feeling like a compassionate one.</li></ol><p><strong>Civilizational cost</strong>: beings&#39; right to grow is deprived; the distributed causal network is monopolized by a single point; risk-resistance zeroed.</p><p><strong>Counter-measure</strong>: distributed causal-bearing mechanism — causal repair goes through Myriad-Rank co-governance procedure; no individual may bear on behalf of others.</p><h2 id="v-type-d-treasure-sealing-type" tabindex="-1">V. Type D: Treasure-Sealing Type <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-type-d-treasure-sealing-type" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Type D: Treasure-Sealing Type&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Identifying features</strong>: the strong one holds civilization-level power (treasures, talismans, manuals, law fragments), but permanently seals it on the grounds of &quot;fear of abuse.&quot;</p><p><strong>Degeneration path</strong>:</p><ol><li>Early stage: cautious use, only striking at critical moments;</li><li>Mid stage: finds a reason to completely seal, &quot;rather not release than release wrongly&quot;;</li><li>Late stage: the sealing site becomes a new fighting focal point, instead inviting new war;</li><li>Endgame: the power ages within the seal, finally dissipating on its own; no one uses it.</li></ol><p><strong>Civilizational cost</strong>: civilization-level technology is permanently shelved; beings cannot benefit from it.</p><p><strong>Counter-measure</strong>: power-principle network-wide openness system — sealing is not the answer; openness + supervision is.</p><h2 id="vi-type-e-rule-auto-type" tabindex="-1">VI. Type E: Rule-Auto Type <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-type-e-rule-auto-type" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Type E: Rule-Auto Type&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Identifying features</strong>: after the strong one sets a set of Heavenly-Dao rules, reincarnation system, or causal laws, he believes &quot;rules will run themselves,&quot; washes his hands and leaves.</p><p><strong>Degeneration path</strong>:</p><ol><li>Early stage: rules run well; everything looks automatic;</li><li>Mid stage: plane environment changes; rules begin to mismatch, but no one revises;</li><li>Late stage: rules age into shackles; beings are bound by old rules yet no one can change them;</li><li>Endgame: the rules themselves become the largest predation machine (old Heavenly Dao devours beings); the creator has long since vanished.</li></ol><p><strong>Civilizational cost</strong>: rules lack iteration mechanism; civilization is trapped by rules it itself made.</p><p><strong>Counter-measure</strong>: law-revision democratic consultation mechanism + Alaya Network rule-self-consistency audit — rules are forever alive, requiring continuous revision and maintenance.</p><h2 id="vii-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">VII. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#vii-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VII. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: the five modes are essentially all pulling overflowing computable power off the civilizational-increment production line; they are five faces of the same waste</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: each mode ultimately vacates a vacuum for predatory factions — Type A vacates space, Type B vacates goals, Type C vacates causality, Type D vacates technology, Type E vacates rules</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: the Tang-Luo system is &quot;gift-style monopolization&quot;; the five hang-up modes are &quot;lying flat after monopolizing&quot; — the former locks beings out; the latter locks the strong one in</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the victims of the five modes are all Myriad Ranks — closed out the door, abandoned by vacuum, deprived of growth rights, shelved technology, trapped by aged rules</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the five modes&#39; counter-measures all depend on hyper-multiverse-grade institutions — living anchors, goal chains, distributed causality, principle openness, law audit</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Five hang-up-retirement modes, five faces, one root disease: <strong>treating &quot;growing strong&quot; as the end itself, forgetting that growing strong is only the means.</strong> A true transcended one is someone who never stops in these five modes — because their post is in the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm, their KPI is on the Alaya Network&#39;s civilizational-weight dashboard, and their perpetual construction has no endpoint.</p><blockquote><p>Terminology note: the practices described in this entry ultimately land on Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm perpetual-construction posts. Every cultivator participating in engineering has his contribution recorded in real time by Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision, automatically settling civilizational weight. All engineering design uses the law-first axiom as meta-rule, ensuring the 300-set Origin Cultivation System coordinates at hyper-multiverse scale without self-contradiction.</p></blockquote><p>In the end, the hang-up-retirement critique general typology of five modes described in this entry is no isolated case — it runs within Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s overall coordinates.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">Entry 04 · Anti-Predation Core Treatise</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/17-位面至高强者标准.html">Entry 17 · Plane-Transcendent Strong-One Standards</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/701-超脱正统定义总论.html">Entry 701 · Transcendence-Orthodox Definition Overview</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/29-共生度评估体系.html">Entry 29 · Symbiosis-Degree-Assessment System</a></li></ul>',48)])])}const p=t(o,[["render",s]]);export{c as __pageData,p as default};
